//datasheets.tdx.henkel.com/LOCTITE-HY-4070-en_GL.pdf","viscosityClass":"high","name":"HY 4070","viscosityValue":"200-1300","unpublishedFields":["potLife","thermalConductivity"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Etched aluminum, 0.5 mm gap, TDS typical value","applicationTags":["structural-bonding","plastic-repair"],"cureFamily":"Cyanoacrylate / acrylic hybrid","serviceMax":100,"referenceUrl":"https://datasheets.tdx.henkel.com/LOCTITE-HY-4070-en_GL.pdf","viscosityUnit":"mPa.s","lapShear":25,"viscosityNote":"Casson Viscosity Part A, Cone & Plate Rheometer, 25\u00b0C","fixtureTime":1,"gapFill":5,"cautions":["Use LOCTITE cyanoacrylate mixing nozzle for best application results.","Designed for bond gaps up to 5 mm; fixture-time value is for etched aluminum with 0.5 mm gap.","Official public sources do not publish pot life, thermal conductivity or mixed clarity."],"maker":"Henkel Loctite","cureDetail":"Two-part room-temperature hybrid adhesive, 10:1 mix ratio. Fixture time is less than 60 s on etched aluminum at 23 C with 0.5 mm gap; designed for bond gaps up to 5 mm.","thixotropic":true,"id":"loctite-hy4070","environment":{"humidity":0.55,"fuel":0.45,"immersion":0.35,"temperature":0.55},"summary":"Fast-fixturing hybrid bonder for dissimilar materials when standard instant adhesives cannot bridge the joint."},{"profile":"siliconeRubberAdhesive","tensileStrengthPsi":120,"clarity":"transparent","fullCureMinutes":1440,"potLife":"\u226445 min","tdsDocumentLabel":"LOCTITE SI 595 Technical Data Sheet, January 2018; PDF digitally signed by tdx.henkel.com November 27, 2025","serviceMin":null,"sourceRevisionDate":"LOCTITE SI 595 Technical Data Sheet, January 2018; PDF digitally signed by tdx.henkel.com November 27, 2025","fullCureProfiles":[{"temperatureC":23,"minutes":45,"context":"maximum tack-free / surface cure time"},{"temperatureC":23,"minutes":1440,"context":"full cure time"},{"temperatureC":23,"minutes":10080,"context":"cured-material physical properties after 1 week at room temperature"}],"substrates":{"ceramic":8,"composite":7,"glass":9,"aluminum":8,"steel":8,"plastic":7,"electronics":8,"ductwork":8,"windowsDoors":8},"thermalConductivity":null,"tensileStrength":">=0.8 N/mm2 / >=120 psi, ISO 37, cured 1 week at room temperature","stress":{"shear":3,"peel":5,"impact":7},"tdsUrl":"https://datasheets.tdx.henkel.com/LOCTITE-SI-595-en_GL.pdf","viscosityClass":"high","chemistry":"Acetoxy silicone","name":"SI 595","unpublishedFields":["serviceMin","thermalConductivity","viscosityValue","viscosityUnit"],"lapShearSubstrate":"The January 2018 TDS does not publish lap-shear strength; it describes the product as a flexible adhesive sealant and publishes tensile, elongation and hardness.","applicationTags":["sealing-gasketing","electronics-assembly","electrical-insulation","flexible-bonding","rtv-silicone","uv-weathering-resistant"],"appearance":"Clear thixotropic paste","cureFamily":"One-part acetoxy RTV silicone adhesive sealant","paintable":false,"serviceMax":204,"referenceUrl":"https://datasheets.tdx.henkel.com/LOCTITE-SI-595-en_GL.pdf","viscosityUnit":"thixotropic paste","lapShear":18.6,"fixtureTime":30,"specificGravity":1.01,"tensileStrengthMPa":0.8,"gapFill":6,"cautions":["Not recommended for use in pure oxygen or oxygen-rich systems.","Should not be selected as a sealant for chlorine or other strong oxidizing materials.","Henkel states it is designed for superior bonding and sealing to most surfaces but is not recommended for concrete.","Moisture curing begins immediately after exposure to atmosphere; bonding assemblies should be mated immediately after dispensing.","Material removed from containers may be contaminated during use and should not be returned to the original container.","The TDS does not publish service-temperature minimum, pot life, lap shear, dielectric properties, volume resistivity, thermal conductivity or chemical-resistance tables."],"maker":"Henkel Loctite","cureDetail":"One-component RTV silicone cures on exposure to atmospheric moisture. TDS tack-free time is <=45 minutes and full cure time is 24 hours; full performance properties are evaluated after 1 week at room temperature.","thixotropic":true,"id":"loctite-si595","environment":{"humidity":0.8,"fuel":0.15,"immersion":0.35},"summary":"General-purpose RTV silicone adhesive sealant for flexible sealing and bonding through heat, UV, and thermal cycling."},{"profile":"uvAcrylate","clarity":"transparent","tdsDocumentLabel":"LOCTITE AA 3492 Technical Data Sheet, November 2014; PDF digitally signed by tdx.henkel.com November 26, 2025","sourceRevisionDate":"LOCTITE AA 3492 Technical Data Sheet, November 2014; PDF digitally signed by tdx.henkel.com November 26, 2025","substrates":{"glass":10,"steel":8,"aluminum":8,"stainlessSteel":7,"g10Epoxyglass":8,"pvc":7,"abs":6,"polycarbonate":6,"acrylic":6,"automotiveLighting":9},"thermalConductivity":null,"temperatureTestedMaxC":149,"stress":{"shear":6,"peel":7,"impact":6},"tdsUrl":"https://datasheets.tdx.henkel.com/LOCTITE-AA-3492-en_GL.pdf","viscosityClass":"low","chemistry":"One-part modified acrylate","name":"AA 3492","viscosityValue":"350-600","unpublishedFields":["serviceMin","serviceMax","potLife","thermalConductivity"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Glass-to-glass lap shear strength, ISO 4587, from Henkel TDS.","applicationTags":["optical-bonding","glass-bonding","uv-curing","potting","sealing","self-leveling","automotive-lighting","humidity-resistant"],"cureFamily":"UV acrylic","referenceUrl":"https://datasheets.tdx.henkel.com/LOCTITE-AA-3492-en_GL.pdf","viscosityUnit":"mPa.s / cP","lapShear":4.1,"fixtureTime":0.02,"specificGravity":1.03,"tensileStrengthMPa":36.6,"cautions":["The Henkel TDS does not publish a continuous service-temperature range; heat ageing at 121 C and 149 C is retained as test data rather than encoded as serviceMax.","This product is light sensitive; exposure to daylight, UV light and artificial lighting should be minimized during storage and handling.","Henkel recommends black feedlines for dispensing.","Cure rate depends on lamp intensity, distance from light source, required depth of cure or bondline gap, and UV transmittance of the substrate.","Recommended adhesive-cure intensity is 40 mW/cm2 minimum at the bondline with exposure time 5-6 times the fixture time at the same intensity.","Tack-free surface cure for coating, potting or tacking requires higher intensity UV of at least 100 mW/cm2.","Provide cooling for temperature-sensitive thermoplastics.","Plastic grades should be checked for liquid-adhesive stress-cracking risk.","Excess uncured adhesive can be wiped away with organic solvent such as acetone.","Not recommended for pure oxygen or oxygen-rich systems, or as a sealant for chlorine or other strong oxidizing materials.","Store unopened dry at 8 to 21 C; storage below 8 C or above 28 C can adversely affect product properties."],"maker":"Henkel Loctite","cureDetail":"One-part modified acrylate that cures in seconds under 365 nm UV light; fixture time is defined in the TDS as time to 0.1 N/mm2 shear strength on glass microscope slides.","id":"loctite-aa3492","environment":{"humidity":0.95,"immersion":0.9,"temperature":0.8,"dishwasherCycles":0.8},"summary":"Transparent low-viscosity one-part modified-acrylate UV adhesive with exact Henkel TDS data: 350-600 mPa.s viscosity, 1-20 s glass fixture depending on 365 nm intensity, 4.1 MPa glass-glass lap shear, 8.3 MPa steel-glass block shear, 8.8 N/mm glass peel, Shore D 79 hardness and strong humidity, immersion and dishwasher-cycle retention."},{"profile":"thermalEpoxy","clarity":"opaque","potLife":null,"serviceMin":18,"sourceRevisionDate":"CEMEDINE SX-TCA series official English product data page, crawled April 2026","substrates":{"hardPvc":6,"polycarbonate":6,"polystyrene":5,"abs":6,"acrylic":6,"nylon6":5,"steel":6,"aluminum":7,"heatSinks":9,"electronics":9,"verticalSurfaces":8},"thermalConductivity":1.7,"stress":{"shear":4,"peel":3,"impact":5},"viscosityClass":"high","chemistry":"Special acrylic-modified polymer, one-component thermal conductive elastic adhesive","name":"SX1008","viscosityValue":120,"unpublishedFields":["serviceMin","serviceMax","potLife","surfaceResistivityOhm","insulationResistanceOhm","peelStrengthNPerM","chipBondStrengthMPa","cureDepthMm","cureProfiles"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Aluminum/alumite tensile shear after 23 C / 50% RH x 7 d; full substrate table retained in shearStrengthsMPa.","applicationTags":["potting-thermal","electronics-thermal-management","curable-grease","siloxane-free","pump-out-resistant","vibration-resistant","rohs-compliant"],"cureFamily":"Thermally conductive elastic adhesive","serviceMax":30,"referenceUrl":"https://www.cemedine.co.jp/global/en/technology/elastic/sxtca/index.html","viscosityUnit":"Pa.s","lapShear":2.85,"serviceTemperatureNote":"No explicit service temp range; heat aging data at 120\u2013130 \u00b0C (up to 18 weeks); thermal shock \u221240 to +125 \u00b0C (3000 cycles); standard test conditions 16\u201327 \u00b0C.","fixtureTime":3,"tensileStrengthMPa":2.5,"cautions":["CEMEDINE positions this as a curable thermal interface / adhesive, not as a rigid structural epoxy.","Reference page lists made-to-order packaging for SX1008.","The page does not publish a continuous service-temperature range or pot life for SX1008; heat-aging data is reported separately at 120 C and 130 C on aluminum.","Open time for SX1008 and SX1010 is listed as no open-time in the substrate shear test condition.","CEMEDINE reports low-molecular-silicone-free behavior to reduce electrical contact-failure risk, but users must validate contamination sensitivity in the actual device."],"maker":"CEMEDINE","cureDetail":"One-component special acrylic-modified polymer moisture-curing elastic adhesive. Official test condition for adhesive-property data is 23 C / 50% RH x 7 days; skin-over time is 3 min at 23 C.","id":"cemedine-sx1008","environment":{"humidity":0.75,"fuel":0.35,"immersion":0.4,"temperature":0.75},"summary":"One-part thermally conductive elastic adhesive for electronics heat-management joints where pump-out resistance and vibration durability matter."},{"profile":"siliconeRubberAdhesive","clarity":"opaque","potLife":null,"serviceMin":-60,"sourceRevisionDate":"CEMEDINE Super X / SX720 Series official English product data page, crawled April 2026","substrates":{"circuitBoards":9,"capacitors":9,"coils":9,"powerSupplies":9,"transformers":9,"electronicComponents":9,"metal":7,"plastic":7,"ceramic":7,"rubber":6,"waterproofSeals":8},"stress":{"shear":5,"peel":4,"impact":6},"viscosityClass":"high","chemistry":"Special polymer containing silyl group, one-component elastic adhesive","name":"SX720","viscosityValue":42,"unpublishedFields":["potLife","thermalConductivity","surfaceResistivityOhm","insulationResistanceOhm","dielectricBreakdownVPerMil","dielectricBreakdownKVPerMm","chipBondStrengthMPa","cureDepthMm","cureProfiles"],"lapShearSubstrate":"SX720W tensile shear strength; CEMEDINE Super X table also publishes broad substrate shear data for the family.","applicationTags":["sealing-gasketing","potting-thermal","electronics-assembly","flame-retardant","ul94-v0","siloxane-free","halogen-free","antimony-free","phosphorus-free","waterproofing"],"cureFamily":"Elastic adhesive","serviceMax":120,"referenceUrl":"https://www.cemedine.co.jp/global/en/technology/elastic/superx/","viscosityUnit":"Pa.s","lapShear":4,"fixtureTime":9,"specificGravity":1.59,"tensileStrengthMPa":3.8,"cautions":["Reference page describes the SX720 family rather than a single viscosity grade.","UL94 V-0 listing applies to the SX720 series configurations shown by CEMEDINE.","The page does not publish thermal conductivity for SX720; it is an electronics elastic sealing/fixing adhesive, not the thermally conductive SX-TCA line.","SX720 is siloxane-free with no D3-D10 low-molecular cyclosiloxane, but users should still validate electrical contact compatibility in the finished assembly.","For non-porous materials and heavy or vertical parts, CEMEDINE describes double-sided application/contact-bond style use rather than relying only on wet assembly."],"maker":"CEMEDINE","cureDetail":"One-part room-temperature moisture-cure elastic adhesive. CEMEDINE describes pressure-sensitive range about 10 min after application for Super X; SX720W skin-over time is 9 min at 23 C.","id":"cemedine-sx720","environment":{"humidity":0.75,"fuel":0.3,"immersion":0.6,"temperature":0.7},"summary":"Flame-retardant one-part elastic adhesive aimed at electronic component fixing, sealing, and insulation work."},{"profile":"siliconeRubberAdhesive","clarity":"opaque","sourceRevisionDate":"Shin-Etsu Silicone global product notice: High adhesion strength one-component heat cure RTV silicone rubber KE-8100","substrates":{"aluminum":9,"pbt":9,"pps":9,"electronicsSealing":9,"automotiveParts":9},"lapShearProfilesMPa":{"aluminumAluminum":4.1,"pbtPbt":4,"ppsPps":4},"stress":{"shear":7,"peel":3,"impact":5},"viscosityClass":"high","chemistry":"One-component heat-cure RTV silicone rubber adhesive","name":"KE-8100","viscosityValue":120,"unpublishedFields":["serviceMin","serviceMax","potLife","thermalConductivity","volumeResistivityOhmM","surfaceResistivityOhm","connectionResistanceOhm","insulationResistanceOhm","dielectricConstant","dissipationFactor","dielectricBreakdownVPerMil","dielectricBreakdownKVPerMm","elongationPct","peelStrengthNPerM","chipBondStrengthMPa","cureDepthMm","tackFreeTime"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Tensile lap-shear strength after 120 C x 1 h cure: Al/Al 4.1 MPa, PBT/PBT 4.0 MPa, PPS/PPS 4.0 MPa.","applicationTags":["sealing-gasketing","potting-thermal","electronics","automotive","heat-cure-silicone","plastic-housing"],"appearance":"Gray paste before curing","cureFamily":"Heat-cure RTV silicone","referenceUrl":"https://www.shinetsusilicone-global.com/products/notice/157/index.shtml","viscosityUnit":"Pa.s at 23 C","lapShear":4.1,"fixtureTime":60,"tensileStrengthMPa":7.1,"cautions":["Reference page positions KE-8100 as a heat-cure product; it is not a room-temperature-fix silicone.","Lap-shear values are given on specific substrate pairs rather than a generic ASTM family average.","Shin-Etsu states the table values are not specified values.","The official product notice does not publish service-temperature range, pot life, peel strength, elongation, dielectric breakdown, volume resistivity, thermal conductivity, shelf life or storage temperature."],"maker":"Shin-Etsu Silicone","cureDetail":"One-part heat-cure RTV silicone rubber adhesive; standard curing condition is 120 C x 1 h.","id":"shinetsu-ke8100","environment":{"heat":0.75,"cold":0.75,"weathering":0.75,"electricalInsulation":0.8},"summary":"Gray one-component heat-cure RTV silicone adhesive with 4.0 MPa-class tensile lap-shear on aluminum, PBT and PPS for electronics sealing and automotive parts."},{"profile":"siliconeRubberAdhesive","clarity":"opaque","potLife":null,"tdsDocumentLabel":"WACKER SEMICOSIL 9720 TC Technical Data Sheet, most recent change January 7, 2025","serviceMin":-50,"sourceRevisionDate":"WACKER SEMICOSIL 9720 TC Technical Data Sheet, most recent change January 7, 2025","substrates":{"metal":8,"electronics":8,"heatSinks":9,"circuitBoards":7},"thermalConductivity":1.9,"stress":{"shear":3,"peel":2,"impact":4,"thermalTransfer":8},"tdsUrl":"https://www.wacker.com/h/en-us/medias/SEMICOSIL-9720-TC-en-2025.01.07.pdf","viscosityClass":"high","name":"SEMICOSIL 9720 TC","viscosityValue":110000,"unpublishedFields":["potLife","lapShear","volumeResistivityOhmM","surfaceResistivityOhm","connectionResistanceOhm","insulationResistanceOhm","dielectricConstant","dissipationFactor","dielectricBreakdownVPerMil","tensileStrengthMPa","elongationPct","peelStrengthNPerM","chipBondStrengthMPa","cureDepthMm","tackFreeTime"],"applicationTags":["potting-thermal","electronics-assembly","thermal-interface","heat-sink-bonding","addition-cure-silicone"],"cureFamily":"Thermally curable silicone adhesive","serviceMax":180,"referenceUrl":"https://www.wacker.com/h/en-us/medias/SEMICOSIL-9720-TC-en-2025.01.07.pdf","viscosityUnit":"mPa.s","lapShear":null,"fixtureTime":10,"cautions":["Addition-curing silicone; check application fitness by preliminary trials.","General hygiene regulations should be observed.","Storage is at least 3 months cool and dry in the originally sealed container; properties must be checked if stored beyond the label date.","The official TDS does not publish pot life or lap-shear strength for SEMICOSIL 9720 TC.","Appearance is white/opaque, not optically clear."],"maker":"WACKER / SEMICOSIL","cureDetail":"One-part addition-curing heat-cure silicone adhesive","thixotropic":true,"id":"wacker-semicosil-9720tc","environment":{"humidity":0.65,"temperature":0.85,"electricalInsulation":0.8},"summary":"Thermally conductive one-part silicone adhesive for bonding electronic components to heat sinks and other heat-spreading hardware."},{"profile":"structuralAcrylic","clarity":"transparent","fullCureMinutes":1440,"potLife":6,"serviceMin":-50,"mixRatio":"1:1 by weight","sourceRevisionDate":"WEICON Easy-Mix PE-PP 50 Structural Acrylic Adhesive TDS, issued April 29, 2025","substrates":{"pe":9,"peHd":9,"ldpe":8,"polypropylene":9,"tpe":8,"ptfe":6,"pvc":8,"polyamide":6,"polycarbonate":7,"abs":5,"pmma":7,"cfrp":8,"gfrp":9,"galvanizedSteel":7,"stainlessSteel":8,"aluminum":8},"thermalConductivity":null,"stress":{"shear":6,"peel":4,"impact":7},"viscosityClass":"high","chemistry":"Two-component methyl methacrylate structural acrylic adhesive with integrated primer","name":"Easy-Mix PE-PP 50","viscosityValue":20000,"unpublishedFields":["thermalConductivity"],"lapShearSubstrate":"DIN EN 1465 lap shear at 1.5 mm material thickness: steel 1.0338 sandblasted 12 MPa; stainless V2A 11 MPa; aluminum 12 MPa; PE-HD 12 MPa; PP 8 MPa.","applicationTags":["structural-bonding","plastic-repair","low-surface-energy-plastics","methyl-methacrylate","transparent-bonding","no-primer-required"],"appearance":"Transparent pasty adhesive","cureFamily":"Two-part structural acrylic for low-surface-energy plastics","serviceMax":80,"referenceUrl":"https://media.weicon.de/fmds/307156/dld%3Ainline","viscosityUnit":"mPa.s mixture","lapShear":12,"potLifeRangeMinutes":[6,6],"fixtureTime":12,"specificGravity":1,"gapFill":1,"cautions":["The TDS specifications and recommendations are not guaranteed product characteristics; users must run adequate lab and practical tests for the application.","Clean and dry bonding surfaces are essential; WEICON recommends cleaning/degreasing with WEICON Surface Cleaner and mechanical roughening for smooth surfaces.","The first 5 cm of adhesive bead from the static mixer should be discarded.","The adhesive is applied to just one side.","Larger batch quantities cure faster; temperatures below +16 C significantly increase pot life/cure time and from approximately +5 C and below no reaction takes place.","The TDS does not publish thermal conductivity, dielectric properties, chemical-resistance table or detailed shelf-life conditions beyond room/refrigerated minimum shelf life."],"maker":"WEICON","cureDetail":"Easy-Mix 1:1 adhesive. Pot life is 6 min for a 10 ml batch at 20 C, handling strength is 12 min at 35% strength and final strength is 24 h. Higher temperatures reduce pot life and curing time; each +10 C above room temperature approximately halves pot life and curing time. Below +16 C cure slows significantly and from approximately +5 C and below no reaction takes place.","thixotropic":true,"id":"weicon-easy-mix-pe-pp-50","environment":{"humidity":0.5,"fuel":0.55,"immersion":0.35},"summary":"Transparent structural acrylic designed for low-surface-energy plastics such as PE, PP, and TPE without separate priming.","shortTermServiceTemperatureMaxC":100},{"profile":"thinCA","clarity":"transparent","sourceRevisionDate":"CEMEDINE 3000 Series official English product data page, crawled April 2026","substrates":{"steel":7,"aluminum":7,"copper":7,"chromiumPlatedSteel":7,"abs":6,"acrylic":5,"polystyrene":5,"pvc":6,"bakelite":7,"nylon":6,"polycarbonate":7,"naturalRubber":5,"chloropreneRubber":5,"sbr":5,"nitrileRubber":5,"epdm":4,"tpe":5,"electronics":7,"precisionParts":7},"stress":{"shear":5,"peel":1,"impact":1},"viscosityClass":"low","chemistry":"Ethyl-2-cyanoacrylate","name":"3000RX","viscosityValue":3,"unpublishedFields":["serviceMin","serviceMax","potLife","thermalConductivity","surfaceResistivityOhm","connectionResistanceOhm","insulationResistanceOhm","tensileStrengthMPa","elongationPct","hardnessValue","hardnessScale","peelStrengthNPerM","chipBondStrengthMPa","cureDepthMm","cureProfiles"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Steel tensile shear strength; full 3000RX substrate table retained in shearStrengthsMPa.","applicationTags":["instant-bonding","electronics-assembly","rubber-bonding","precision-assembly","threadlock-light-duty","porous-material-repair","solvent-free"],"cureFamily":"Cyanoacrylate","referenceUrl":"https://www.cemedine.co.jp/global/en/technology/cyanoacrylates/3000/index.html","viscosityUnit":"mPa.s","lapShear":13,"fixtureTime":0.1,"specificGravity":"1.21-1.25","cautions":["CEMEDINE publishes 3000RX as a super-quick curing instant adhesive; values are product data, not a guarantee for every production joint.","Several plastic and rubber shear entries are marked with material failure; the listed strength can be limited by the substrate rather than adhesive cohesion.","The page does not publish continuous service temperature, thermal conductivity, chemical resistance or long-term environmental aging data for 3000RX.","Cyanoacrylate cure depends on surface moisture, bondline gap and substrate chemistry; confirm set time on actual production parts."],"maker":"CEMEDINE","cureDetail":"One-part ethyl-2-cyanoacrylate instant adhesive that polymerizes from trace moisture on the adherend surface. CEMEDINE publishes 3000RX set time as 5 s at 23 C and substrate-specific set times from 1-10 s.","id":"cemedine-3000rx","environment":{"humidity":0.45,"fuel":0.25,"immersion":0.2},"summary":"Super-quick curing ethyl cyanoacrylate for electric/electronic parts, rubber, precision assemblies and porous repair work, with official 3000RX set-time, substrate shear and electrical insulation data."},{"profile":"structuralAcrylic","clarity":"transparent","fullCureMinutes":1440,"potLife":5,"serviceMin":-20,"mixRatio":"4:1 by weight","sandable":true,"sourceRevisionDate":"WEICON VA 2407 Cyanoacrylate Adhesive TDS, issued February 18, 2026","substrates":{"polycarbonate":9,"plastic":8,"steel":9,"stainlessSteel":8,"aluminum":8,"ceramics":8,"glass":8,"rubber":8,"plexiglas":8,"pvc":8,"abs":8},"thermalConductivity":0.1,"stress":{"shear":7,"peel":4,"impact":7},"viscosityClass":"medium","chemistry":"Two-component ethyl acrylate cyanoacrylate adhesive","name":"VA 2407","viscosityValue":1000,"lapShearSubstrate":"DIN EN 1465 shear strength: steel sandblasted 16-21 MPa, aluminum sandblasted 10-15 MPa, rigid untreated PVC 10-14 MPa, untreated ABS 13-15 MPa and polycarbonate 12-17 MPa.","applicationTags":["structural-bonding","plastic-repair","cyanoacrylate","transparent-bonding","rubber-bonding","fast-fixturing","gap-filling"],"appearance":"Transparent pasty adhesive","cureFamily":"Two-component cyanoacrylate structural adhesive","paintable":true,"serviceMax":120,"referenceUrl":"https://media.weicon.de/fmds/376908/dld:inline","viscosityUnit":"mPa.s at 25 C, cone/plate","lapShear":16,"fixtureTime":1.4,"specificGravity":1.1,"gapFill":5,"cautions":["The TDS specifications and recommendations are not guaranteed product characteristics; users must run adequate lab and practical tests for the application.","Successful application depends on thorough surface preparation.","Use physical, safety, toxicological and ecological data from WEICON EC safety data sheets when applying.","The TDS does not publish detailed chemical-resistance tables despite product-page statements about resistance to many aggressive chemicals.","Scalar lapShear uses the lower bound for steel; full substrate ranges are preserved in shearStrengthsMPa.","Do not count generic dielectric strength or volume resistivity as electronics-performance evidence; the TDS does not position this as a PCB, potting, conformal coating, conductive adhesive, die-attach, or electronics assembly adhesive."],"maker":"WEICON","cureDetail":"4:1 two-component cyanoacrylate adhesive. Initial adhesion is measured at 23 C / 50% RH to 0.5 MPa shear strength: about 4 s on sandblasted aluminum, 84 s on untreated ABS and 55 s on rigid PVC. Pot life is 5 min at 20 C for a 10 g batch and final strength is reached after 24 h.","id":"weicon-va2407","environment":{"humidity":0.55,"fuel":0.45,"immersion":0.35},"summary":"Transparent two-component hybrid adhesive for visually clean structural bonds on plastics, metal, ceramics, glass, and rubber."},{"profile":"toughenedEpoxy","potLife":150,"productSku":"10056568","serviceMin":-50,"mixRatio":"2:1 by volume","sourceRevisionDate":"WEICON Easy-Mix HT 250 Epoxy Adhesive Technical Data Sheet, issued February 18, 2026","substrates":{"steel":10,"aluminum":9,"abs":6,"polycarbonate":5,"carbonFiber":7,"fr4":7},"thermalConductivity":1.4,"lapShearProfilesMPa":{"steel10338Sandblasted":20,"aluminiumSandblasted":15,"abs":6,"polycarbonate":4,"gfrp":10},"stress":{"shear":5,"peel":2,"impact":3},"viscosityClass":"high","potLifeConditions":"150 min at 20 C for a 10 ml batch; larger batches and higher temperatures shorten pot life.","chemistry":"Two-component epoxy resin adhesive","name":"Easy-Mix HT 250","viscosityValue":38000,"unpublishedFields":["clarity","volumeResistivityOhmM","surfaceResistivityOhm","insulationResistanceOhm","dielectricConstant","dissipationFactor","peelStrengthNPerM","chipBondStrengthMPa","cureDepthMm","tackFreeTime"],"lapShearSubstrate":"DIN EN 1465, 1.5 mm material thickness: steel 1.0338 sandblasted 20 MPa, aluminium sandblasted 15 MPa, ABS 6 MPa, PC 4 MPa, GFRP 10 MPa.","shelfLifeMonths":18,"applicationTags":["structural-bonding","potting-thermal","high-temperature","powder-coating","thermally-conductive","electrically-insulating"],"cureFamily":"Epoxy","serviceMax":200,"referenceUrl":"https://media.weicon.de/fmds/307151/dld%3Ainline","viscosityUnit":"mPa.s","lapShear":20,"applicationTemperatureMaxC":40,"applicationTemperatureMinC":10,"fixtureTime":480,"tensileStrengthMPa":50,"gapFill":4,"cautions":["WEICON states continuous temperature resistance to 200 C and brief exposure only to 250 C.","Discard the first 5 cm from the static mixer before use.","Pot life and cure time are batch-size and temperature dependent; every 10 C increase above room temperature roughly halves them, temperatures below 16 C slow them significantly, and from about 5 C and below no reaction takes place.","For permanently high temperature resistance, anneal at 80 C for 30 min after 24 h room-temperature cure.","Store unopened cartridges dry at 18 to 25 C away from direct sunlight; failure to follow storage instructions can reduce shelf life to 6 months.","Epoxy resin crystallization below 5 C can harm processing/cure/technical data but may be reversed by heating up to max 50 C without open flame."],"maker":"WEICON","cureDetail":"Two-component epoxy resin system. Apply from the 50 ml 2:1 double cartridge through a static mixer after discarding the first 5 cm of bead. Pot life is 150 min for a 10 ml batch at 20 C; 50% working strength is reached after 8 h and full strength after 24 h or after 30 min at 80 C. For permanent high-temperature resistance, WEICON recommends annealing at 80 C for 30 min after 24 h.","id":"weicon-easy-mix-ht250","environment":{"humidity":0.75,"fuel":0.75,"immersion":0.65},"summary":"High-temperature light-gray two-part epoxy with exact WEICON TDS data: 2:1 mix, 38,000 mPa.s viscosity, 4 mm gap bridging, 150 min pot life, 20 MPa steel lap shear, 1.4 W/m.K thermal conductivity, >24 kV/mm dielectric strength and -50 to 200 C continuous service with brief 250 C exposure.","shortTermServiceTemperatureMaxC":250},{"profile":"siliconeRubberAdhesive","clarity":"opaque","productSku":"10067875","serviceMin":-40,"sourceRevisionDate":"WEICON Flex 310 M Hybrid Technical Data Sheet, issue date April 23, 2026","substrates":{"powderCoatedMetal":9,"galvanisedMetal":9,"anodisedMetal":9,"chromatedMetal":8,"hotDipGalvanisedMetal":9,"metal":8,"plastics":7,"naturalStone":8,"concrete":7,"masonry":7,"plaster":6,"wood":7,"glass":8},"thermalConductivity":null,"stress":null,"viscosityClass":"high","chemistry":"One-component MS-polymer / SMP adhesive and sealant","name":"Flex 310 M Hybrid","unpublishedFields":["serviceMin","serviceMax","potLife","thermalConductivity","stress","viscosityValue","viscosityUnit"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Medium lap shear strength according to DIN EN 1465 / ASTM D1002 from WEICON TDS.","shelfLifeMonths":12,"applicationTags":["sealing-gasketing","structural-bonding","elastic-bonding","ms-polymer","weather-resistant","electrical-industry","vehicle-construction","tank-apparatus"],"appearance":"Grey pasty adhesive/sealant","cureFamily":"Moisture-curing SMP hybrid adhesive sealant","serviceMax":90,"referenceUrl":"https://media.weicon.de/fmds/466804/dld%3Ainline","lapShear":1.4,"applicationTemperatureMaxC":40,"applicationTemperatureMinC":5,"fixtureTime":10,"tensileStrengthMPa":1.3,"gapFill":5,"cautions":["This is an elastic adhesive/sealant, not a rigid structural epoxy; the TDS lap-shear value is 1.4 MPa.","Bonding parts must be joined before the adhesive skins over.","Surfaces must be clean and free of grease; WEICON recommends Surface Cleaner, Cleaner Spray S for heavily soiled metal, and Sealant and Adhesive Remover for old paint or adhesive residues.","For some materials or special requirements, WEICON recommends a bonding agent / primer, and mechanical roughening can improve adhesion.","Store unopened at room temperature and avoid heat sources and direct sunlight.","The TDS values are laboratory/practical-experience recommendations, not guaranteed product characteristics."],"maker":"WEICON","cureDetail":"One-component neutral cross-linking moisture-cure MS-polymer adhesive/sealant. Processing and cure conditions are +5 to +40 C and 30% to 95% relative humidity; parts must be joined before the 10 min skin-over time.","id":"weicon-flex310m-hybrid","environment":{"humidity":0.85,"uv":0.85,"immersion":0.4,"temperature":0.6},"summary":"Grey one-component SMP/MS-polymer adhesive sealant with exact WEICON TDS data: -40 to 90 C temperature resistance, 5 mm gap bridging, 10 min skin-over, 2-3 mm/24 h cure speed, 1.4 MPa medium lap shear, 1.3 MPa tensile strength, 500% elongation and Shore A 32 hardness."},{"profile":"siliconeRubberAdhesive","clarity":"opaque","productSku":"10067865","serviceMin":-40,"sourceRevisionDate":"WEICON Flex 310 M HT 220+ Technical Data Sheet, issue date April 23, 2026","substrates":{"aluminum":8,"stainlessSteel":8,"metal":9,"powderCoatedMetal":9,"paintedMetal":8,"plastics":7,"glass":7,"vehicleBody":9,"hvacDucting":9,"container":8},"thermalConductivity":null,"stress":{"shear":3,"peel":3,"impact":4},"viscosityClass":"high","chemistry":"One-component MS-polymer / SMP adhesive and sealant","name":"Flex 310 M HT 220+","unpublishedFields":["potLife","thermalConductivity","viscosityValue","viscosityUnit"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Medium lap shear strength according to DIN EN 1465 / ASTM D1002 from WEICON TDS.","shelfLifeMonths":12,"applicationTags":["sealing-gasketing","structural-bonding","elastic-bonding","ms-polymer","high-temperature","weather-resistant","powder-coating","vehicle-construction","hvac","tank-apparatus"],"appearance":"Grey pasty adhesive/sealant","cureFamily":"High-temperature SMP hybrid adhesive sealant","serviceMax":90,"referenceUrl":"https://media.weicon.de/fmds/466827/dld%3Ainline","lapShear":1.6,"applicationTemperatureMaxC":40,"applicationTemperatureMinC":5,"fixtureTime":10,"tensileStrengthMPa":3.4,"cautions":["WEICON specifies +220 C only as a single approx. 30 min excursion and +200 C as 120 min; permanent temperature resistance is -40 to +90 C.","This is an elastic SMP adhesive/sealant, not a rigid structural epoxy; the TDS lap-shear value is 1.6 MPa.","Bonding parts must be joined before the adhesive skins over.","Surfaces must be clean and free of grease; WEICON recommends Surface Cleaner, Cleaner Spray S for heavily soiled metal, and Sealant and Adhesive Remover for old paint or adhesive residues.","For certain materials or special requirements, WEICON recommends a bonding agent / primer, and mechanical roughening can improve adhesion.","After artificial ageing according to DIN ISO 21194 Annex A, Flex 310 M HT 220+ with Primer K 200 or Activating Cleaner achieved grade 2 bead peel on aluminium and stainless steel, meaning 75% to 95% cohesive failure.","Store unopened at room temperature and avoid heat sources and direct sunlight.","The TDS values are laboratory/practical-experience recommendations, not guaranteed product characteristics."],"maker":"WEICON","cureDetail":"One-component moisture-curing, neutral cross-linking MS-polymer adhesive/sealant. Processing and cure conditions are +5 to +40 C and 30% to 95% relative humidity; parts must be joined before the 10 min skin-over time.","id":"weicon-flex310m-ht220plus","serviceExcursions":[{"temperatureC":200,"durationMinutes":120},{"temperatureC":220,"durationMinutes":30}],"environment":{"humidity":0.85,"uv":0.85,"immersion":0.55,"oilGrease":0.75,"diluteAcidAlkali":0.65,"temperature":0.8},"summary":"Grey fast-curing one-component SMP/MS-polymer adhesive sealant with exact WEICON TDS data: -40 to 90 C continuous temperature resistance, short excursions of 120 min at 200 C or 30 min at 220 C, 10 min skin-over, 2-3 mm/24 h cure speed, 1.6 MPa lap shear, 3.4 MPa tensile strength, 160% elongation and Shore A 57 hardness.","shortTermServiceTemperatureMaxC":220},{"profile":"thermalEpoxy","clarity":"Opaque gray cured material","standards":["RoHS Directive 2015/863/EU","IEC 61249-2-21 halogen-free","JEDEC MSL 1 referring to IPC/JEDEC J-STD-020D.1","GB33372-2020 VOC-content limits for adhesives","ASTM D5470 thermal conductivity method","DIN EN 62631-3-1 volume resistivity","DIN EN 62631-3-2 surface resistance","DIN EN ISO 527 tensile properties","DIN EN ISO 868 Shore D hardness"],"potLife":2880,"serviceMin":-40,"sourceRevisionDate":"DELO MONOPOX TC2270 Technical Datasheet, as of 28.10.2024 07:58","substrates":{"fr4":9,"silicon":9,"gold":8,"lcp":7,"abs":7,"pcb":9,"semiconductorDie":10},"thermalConductivity":1.7,"stress":{"shear":8,"peel":2,"impact":4},"viscosityClass":"very-high-viscosity thixotropic paste","potLifeConditions":"DELO TDS calls this a 48 h processing time at +23 C / 50% RH for the one-component product; it is not a mixed two-part pot life.","chemistry":"Modified epoxy resin with aluminum nitride ceramic filler","name":"MONOPOX TC2270","viscosityValue":145000,"unpublishedFields":["fixtureTime","lapShear","surfaceResistivityOhm","insulationResistanceOhm","dielectricConstant","dissipationFactor","dielectricBreakdownVPerMil","dielectricBreakdownKVPerMm","peelStrengthNPerM","cureDepthMm","tackFreeTime"],"shelfLifeMonths":6,"applicationTags":["potting-thermal","die-attach","power-semiconductor","thermally-conductive","electrically-insulating","electronics"],"appearance":"Gray opaque cured material in 1 mm layer thickness","cureFamily":"Heat-cure epoxy","serviceMax":150,"referenceUrl":"https://www.delo-adhesives.com/service-center/downloads/downloads/datasheet/DELO%20MONOPOX_TC2270_TIDB-en.pdf?cHash=466a3e7a101e66f2e24dbbb1c2c49513&show=1&type=5001","viscosityUnit":"mPa.s at 10 1/s shear rate, 500 um gap","tensileStrengthMPa":28,"cautions":["The official TDS reports DELO compression shear and die-shear values, not a standard lap-shear value; lapShear is intentionally left blank.","The 48 h processing-time value is captured as potLife only as a one-component processing-life equivalent, not as a two-component mixed pot life.","Heating time of the components must be added to the published cure time, and the specified cure temperature must be reached directly at the adhesive.","Changing curing temperature, irradiation intensity or cure time can change physical properties.","Depending on adhesive quantity, exothermic reaction heat can cause overheating; DELO advises selecting a lower cure temperature in that case.","The Technical Datasheet states values are typical laboratory values and are not a product specification."],"maker":"DELO","cureDetail":"One-component heat-curing modified epoxy resin. DELO publishes typical cure times of 90 min at +60 C or 15 min at +80 C in an air convection oven; the specified curing temperature must be reached directly at the adhesive.","id":"delo-monopox-tc2270","environment":{"humidity":0.8,"thermalCycling":0.8,"temperature":0.75,"electricalInsulation":0.95},"summary":"Electrically insulating, thermally conductive one-part aluminum-nitride-filled epoxy for power semiconductor die attach and electronic assemblies requiring low-temperature heat cure, JEDEC MSL 1 reliability and high through-bond heat transfer."},{"profile":"thermalEpoxy","clarity":"opaque","potLife":120,"tdsDocumentLabel":"Hoenle/Panacol Elecolit 325 Technical Datasheet, updated September 11, 2025, revision 6","serviceMin":-40,"mixRatio":"1:1","sourceRevisionDate":"Hoenle/Panacol Elecolit 325 Technical Datasheet, updated September 11, 2025, revision 6","substrates":{"electricalContacts":10,"esdDischargePaths":10,"heatSensitiveComponents":9,"electronicComponents":9,"opv":8,"photovoltaics":8,"metals":8,"steel":8},"thermalConductivity":4,"lapShearProfilesMPa":{"steelSteelRoomTemperature24h":[5,10],"steelSteel120C15min":[15,20]},"stress":{"shear":4,"peel":1,"impact":2},"tdsUrl":"https://www.panacol.com/panacol/datasheets/elecolit/elecolit-325-english-tds-panacol-adhesive.pdf","viscosityClass":"paste-like","chemistry":"Silver-filled modified epoxy","name":"Elecolit 325","viscosityValue":"paste-like","unpublishedFields":["surfaceResistivityOhm","connectionResistanceOhm","insulationResistanceOhm","tensileStrengthMPa","elongationPct","peelStrengthNPerM","chipBondStrengthMPa","cureDepthMm","tackFreeTime"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Steel/steel lap shear from Elecolit 325 TDS: 5-10 MPa after room-temperature 24 h cure; 15-20 MPa after 120 C / 15 min cure.","shelfLifeMonths":12,"applicationTags":["potting-thermal","electrically-conductive","silver-filled","conductive-epoxy","esd","electrical-contacting","thermal-management","room-temperature-cure","heat-cure","electronics-assembly"],"cureFamily":"Electrically and thermally conductive two-part epoxy","serviceMax":150,"referenceUrl":"https://www.panacol.com/panacol/datasheets/elecolit/elecolit-325-english-tds-panacol-adhesive.pdf","viscosityUnit":"mixed adhesive; Panacol TDS lists paste-like rather than numeric mPa.s","lapShearRangeMPa":[5,10],"lapShear":7.5,"fixtureTime":960,"cautions":["Electrically conductive ICA material intended for electronic contacting/ESD paths, not insulating bonding.","After thawing once, Elecolit 325 should not be frozen again.","After storage at 0-10 C, homogenize because silver sedimentation is possible.","Avoid condensation during thawing; 30 cc and 50 cc syringes need approximately 1 h thaw time.","Low-surface-energy substrates such as polyethylene and polypropylene must be pretreated.","Published values are typical properties and not product specifications."],"maker":"Panacol","cureDetail":"Mix two components at 1:1 ratio and apply within the 2 h pot life. Typical cure schedules are 16 h at 25 C, 2 h at 50 C, 30 min at 100 C, 15 min at 120 C or 5 min at 150 C. Final bond strength is achieved no sooner than 24 h after bonded components are removed from the oven.","id":"panacol-elecolit-325","environment":{"humidity":0.45,"fuel":0.35,"immersion":0.25},"summary":"Silver-filled two-part solvent-free modified epoxy for electrical contacting and ESD discharge, with 2 h pot life, room-temperature or heat cure, 3.8-4.2 W/m*K thermal conductivity and 1E-4 to 5E-4 Ohm.cm volume resistivity."},{"profile":"siliconeRubberAdhesive","clarity":"translucent","potLife":null,"serviceMin":18,"sourceRevisionDate":"ThreeBond International 1500 Series Elastic & Bonding Adhesives product page, cached April 24, 2026","fullCureProfiles":[{"temperatureC":23,"hoursRange":[12,24],"context":"approx. practical strength / one-half final strength, bond-area dependent"},{"temperatureC":23,"hoursRange":[72,168],"context":"final strength per 1530 Series description"}],"substrates":{"metal":7,"plastic":7,"rubber":8,"wood":7,"inorganicMaterials":7,"siliconeRubber":5,"electronics":6},"thermalConductivity":null,"stress":{"shear":4,"peel":6,"impact":7},"viscosityClass":"high","chemistry":"Silyl-containing special polymer","name":"1530C","viscosityValue":100,"unpublishedFields":["potLife","thermalConductivity"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Iron/iron lap shear strength for TB1530C on ThreeBond 1500 Series product page: 3.5 MPa.","applicationTags":["sealing-gasketing","structural-bonding","flexible-bonding","elastic-adhesive","moisture-cure","electronics-assembly"],"appearance":"Translucent","cureFamily":"One-component solventless moisture-curing elastic adhesive","serviceMax":30,"referenceUrl":"https://threebond.com/products/adhesives/elastic-bonding-adhesives/","viscosityUnit":"Pa.s","lapShear":3.5,"serviceTemperatureNote":"TDS cache is family-level HTML page; 16\u201327 \u00b0C appears to be standard test conditions, not service temperature. Use manufacturer TDS PDF for confirmed service range.","fixtureTime":7,"cautions":["ThreeBond states product-table values are examples of measured values and not guarantee levels.","Before using, confirm adequacy and safety for the relevant application.","The source product page gives product-family data rather than a full downloadable product-specific TDS for 1530C.","The product page does not publish service-temperature minimum, pot life, thermal conductivity, dielectric properties, chemical resistance or shelf life."],"maker":"ThreeBond","cureDetail":"Single-component moisture-curing alcohol-type elastomeric adhesive. The 1530-series description states strong initial tack develops in 5-10 minutes, practical strength can reach about half final strength after 12-24 h depending on bond area, and final strength is reached after 3-7 days.","id":"threebond-1530c","environment":{"humidity":0.65,"fuel":0.2,"immersion":0.35},"summary":"Translucent one-component elastomeric adhesive for general-purpose industrial bonding where flexibility and moisture cure are preferred over rigid bondlines."},{"profile":"siliconeRubberAdhesive","clarity":"opaque","serviceMin":-50,"sourceRevisionDate":"DOWSIL Silicone Sealants and Foams for Industrial, Appliance and Maintenance selection guide, Form No. 80-8283-01","substrates":{"nylon66":10,"polycarbonate":10,"glass":10,"aluminum":10,"copper":10,"galvanizedSteel":10,"lowCarbonSteel":10,"stainlessSteel":10,"acrylic":4,"abs":4,"ldpe":2,"polypropylene":2,"paint":3},"thermalConductivity":null,"stress":{"shear":3,"peel":3,"impact":5,"thermalCycle":7},"viscosityClass":"high","chemistry":"Two-component neutral silicone adhesive/sealant, VMQ sealant type","name":"Dowsil Q3-3526","unpublishedFields":["potLife","lapShear","thermalConductivity","viscosityValue","viscosityUnit"],"applicationTags":["sealing-gasketing","structural-bonding","two-part-silicone","neutral-cure","automotive-lighting","appliance-assembly","heat-resistant"],"cureFamily":"Two-part silicone adhesive sealant","serviceMax":190,"referenceUrl":"https://www.dow.com/documents/80/80-8283-01-silicone-sealants-foams-industrial-assembly.pdf?iframe=true","fixtureTime":20,"specificGravity":"1.32-1.36","tensileStrengthMPa":2,"cautions":["The official Dow selection guide publishes tensile strength but not lap-shear strength for Q3-3526, so lapShear is intentionally omitted.","The guide does not publish thermal conductivity or pot life for Q3-3526.","Most paints will not adhere to silicone sealant.","Not for underwater structural or adhesive applications.","Some plastics may stress-crack; test before use.","Service-temperature ranges are estimated from formulation and laboratory testing; actual service range depends on the application environment.","Primerless adhesion entries marked with an asterisk in the Dow table are encoded as consult Dow rather than treated as positive ratings."],"maker":"Dow / Dupont Silicones","cureDetail":"Two-component neutral silicone adhesive/sealant; fast cure at room temperature with through-cure rather than outside-inward moisture cure. Dow table lists 8 min skin-over and 20 min tack-free time.","id":"dow-q3-3526","environment":{"humidity":0.8,"uv":0.85,"temperature":0.85,"immersion":0.35},"summary":"Fast-curing non-slump two-part silicone adhesive/sealant with exact Dow selection-guide data: -50 to 190 C continuous temperature range, 8 min skin-over, 20 min tack-free, <2 mm flow, Shore A 38-40, 2 MPa tensile strength, 270-280% elongation, 1.32-1.36 specific gravity range and excellent primerless adhesion to nylon, polycarbonate, glass, aluminum, copper and common steels."},{"profile":"siliconeRubberAdhesive","serviceMin":-45,"sourceRevisionDate":"Dow DOWSIL EA-9187L UV Silicone Conformal Coating Technical Data Sheet, Form No. 11-3909-01, 2018","substrates":{"pcb":10,"printedCircuitBoard":10,"electronicComponents":9,"glass":6,"commonSubstrates":7},"stress":{"shear":1,"peel":1,"impact":4},"viscosityClass":"medium","chemistry":"One-part neutral-cure RTV silicone conformal coating","name":"Dowsil EA-9187L","viscosityValue":900,"unpublishedFields":["potLife","fixtureTime","clarity","thermalConductivity","surfaceResistivityOhm","insulationResistanceOhm","peelStrengthNPerM","chipBondStrengthMPa","cureDepthMm","tackFreeTime"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Unprimed lap shear on glass from Dow TDS.","shelfLifeMonths":12,"applicationTags":["conformal-coating","electronics-assembly","pcb-protection","dielectric-protection","uv-indicator","solventless","thin-section-encapsulation"],"cureFamily":"Moisture-cure silicone conformal coating","shortTermServiceTemperatureMinC":-55,"serviceMax":200,"referenceUrl":"https://www.dow.com/en-us/pdp.dowsil-ea-9187l-uv-conformal-coating.04064436z.html","viscosityUnit":"mPa.s / cP","lapShear":0.31,"specificGravity":0.98,"tensileStrengthMPa":0.44,"cautions":["This is a conformal coating / thin-section encapsulant rather than a gap-filling structural adhesive.","Cure depends on method of application, film thickness, temperature and humidity; mild heat at 60 C or less can improve cure times.","Pot life depends on application method; to extend pot life, minimize exposure to ambient moisture with dry air or dry nitrogen blanketing when possible.","Adhesion can lag behind cure and may take up to 72 h at room temperature; test adhesion only after that interval.","Apply to clean, dry substrates; difficult low-surface-energy substrates may need primer, chemical etching or plasma treatment.","Store in original packaging tightly closed, minimize headspace, and prevent moisture contact; purge partially filled containers with dry air or nitrogen.","Useful temperature range is application-dependent; Dow states most silicone adhesives are operational -45 to 200 C for long periods, with possible low-temperature cycling to -55 C only after assembly verification.","Not tested or represented as suitable for medical or pharmaceutical uses.","TDS values are typical and not intended for preparing specifications."],"maker":"Dow / Dupont Silicones","cureDetail":"Flowable one-component neutral-cure RTV silicone conformal coating. Cures with atmospheric moisture at room temperature, with optional mild heat acceleration of 60 C or less; adhesion may take up to 72 h at room temperature to build.","id":"dow-ea-9187l","environment":{"humidity":0.8,"corrosion":0.85,"immersion":0.45,"temperature":0.85},"summary":"One-part translucent solventless UV-indicated silicone conformal coating for high-reliability electronics, with exact Dow TDS values: 900 mPa.s viscosity, 9 min skin-over, 0.44 MPa tensile strength, 165% elongation, 0.31 MPa unprimed glass lap shear, 20 kV/mm dielectric strength, 3E15 ohm.cm volume resistivity and UL 746C / UL 94 V-0 recognition."},{"profile":"siliconeRubberAdhesive","clarity":"opaque","potLife":null,"tdsDocumentLabel":"Three Bond International TB1211 Silicone Sealant Technical Data Sheet, Revision 0.2, February 3, 2003","serviceMin":-60,"sourceRevisionDate":"Three Bond International TB1211 Silicone Sealant Technical Data Sheet, Revision 0.2, issued February 3, 2003; document control 3-TB-20-0418.","substrates":{"flanges":9,"solidSheetGaskets":9,"metal":7,"engineAssemblies":8,"waterPumps":7,"oilPans":7},"thermalConductivity":null,"stress":{"shear":2,"peel":2,"impact":6},"tdsUrl":"https://threebond.com/download/threebond-1211-silicone-sealant","viscosityClass":"high","chemistry":"One-component moisture-curing silicone RTV","name":"1211","viscosityValue":70,"unpublishedFields":["lapShear","potLife","thermalConductivity"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Aluminum/aluminum, room temperature: 1.0 MPa, per the linked TDS.","applicationTags":["sealing-gasketing","liquid-gasket","rtv-silicone","oil-resistant","automotive-aftermarket","small-engine"],"appearance":"White","cureFamily":"One-part moisture-curing silicone liquid gasket","serviceMax":200,"referenceUrl":"https://threebond.com/products/sealants/silicone-rtv/","viscosityUnit":"Pa\u00b7s (700 P), TDS typical uncured value","lapShear":1.0,"serviceTemperatureNote":"The linked 2003 TB1211 TDS lists service temperature -60 to 200 \u00b0C. Confirm current regional formulation before specification.","fixtureTime":90,"specificGravity":1.01,"tensileStrengthMPa":2.5,"cautions":["ThreeBond states product-table values are examples of measured values and not guarantee levels.","Best fit is sealing and liquid-gasket use, not structural load transfer.","Current source exposes tack-free time and blow-out resistance but not a lap-shear strength value.","The source product page does not publish service-temperature range, pot life, thermal conductivity, dielectric properties, chemical resistance or shelf life for TB1211.","TDS is an older February 2003 revision; verify current product formulation and local availability."],"maker":"ThreeBond","cureDetail":"Moisture-cured, room-temperature-vulcanizing silicone sealant. Manufacturer TDS describes FIPG use and reports a 90 minute tack-free time.","id":"threebond-1211","environment":{"humidity":0.7,"fuel":0.6,"immersion":0.45},"summary":"Low-viscosity multipurpose silicone liquid gasket for general sealing and gasketing where flow into narrow joints is useful."},{"profile":"anaerobicRetainer","clarity":"opaque","fullCureMinutes":1440,"potLife":"2-24 h (workable to full cure)","tdsDocumentLabel":"Three Bond International TB1324 Anaerobic Sealant Technical Data Sheet, Rev. 0.1, issued June 17, 2003, document 3-TB-20-0862","serviceMin":18,"sourceRevisionDate":"Three Bond International TB1324 Anaerobic Sealant Technical Data Sheet, Rev. 0.1, issued June 17, 2003, document 3-TB-20-0862","substrates":{"steel":10,"stainlessSteel":8,"aluminum":8,"brass":8,"zincChromate":7,"nickel":8,"threadedFasteners":10},"thermalConductivity":null,"stress":{"shear":6,"peel":1,"impact":3},"tdsUrl":"https://threebond.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/ThreeBond-1324-anaerobic-sealant.pdf","viscosityClass":"medium","chemistry":"Medium-strength anaerobic acrylic sealant / threadlocking adhesive","name":"1324","viscosityValue":650,"unpublishedFields":["serviceMin","serviceMax","fixtureTime","lapShear","thermalConductivity","stress"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Steel fixing shear strength 28 MPa (290 kgf/cm\u00b2) from TB1324 TDS","applicationTags":["threadlocking","retaining","sealing-gasketing","anaerobic","medium-strength","anti-corrosion","metal-bonding"],"cureFamily":"Anaerobic threadlocking and retaining adhesive","serviceMax":30,"referenceUrl":"https://threebond.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/ThreeBond-1324-anaerobic-sealant.pdf","viscosityUnit":"mPa.s / cP","lapShear":28,"fixtureTime":null,"specificGravity":1.13,"gapFill":0.3,"cautions":["Anaerobic adhesive requires metallic contact and oxygen exclusion for cure; it remains uncured in open air.","Torque and shear values are fixture/test-geometry dependent M10 and ThreeBond shear-strength values, not general lap-shear values.","The TDS application sentence says small-diameter removable threaded fasteners, while the current ThreeBond product table positions TB1324 for M10 or larger bolts.","Typical values only, not product specifications.","The TDS does not publish dielectric properties, peel strength, thermal conductivity, shelf life or storage temperature."],"maker":"ThreeBond","cureDetail":"One-part anaerobic adhesive for threaded metal assemblies. Workable cure speed is 2 h and final cure is 24 h; heat cure options are 80 C for 30 min, 100 C for 20 min or 120 C for 10 min.","id":"threebond-1324","environment":{"humidity":0.5,"fuel":0.4,"immersion":0.45},"summary":"Red medium-strength anaerobic sealant/threadlocker with exact ThreeBond TDS data: 650 mPa.s viscosity, 1.13 specific gravity, 2 h workable cure speed, 24 h final cure, 0.3 mm maximum clearance, 28 MPa fixing shear strength and 22 N.m steel M10 breakaway torque."},{"profile":"uvAcrylate","clarity":"transparent","potLife":null,"tdsDocumentLabel":"Hoenle/Panacol Vitralit 6127 Technical Datasheet, updated September 15, 2025, revision 6","serviceMin":-40,"sourceRevisionDate":"Hoenle/Panacol Vitralit 6127 Technical Datasheet, updated September 15, 2025, revision 6","substrates":{"glass":10,"opticalComponents":10,"metal":7,"aluminum":7,"staticGlassObjects":10},"thermalConductivity":0.2,"stress":{"shear":6,"peel":2,"impact":2},"tdsUrl":"https://www.panacol.com/panacol/datasheets/vitralit/vitralit-6127-english-tds-panacol-adhesive.pdf","viscosityClass":"low","chemistry":"Modified acrylate","name":"Vitralit 6127","viscosityValue":"20-100","unpublishedFields":["potLife","volumeResistivityOhmM","surfaceResistivityOhm","insulationResistanceOhm","dissipationFactor","peelStrengthNPerM","chipBondStrengthMPa","cureDepthMm","tackFreeTime"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Glass/aluminum lap shear range from Vitralit 6127 TDS, UV-A Fe-doped hand lamp at 60 mW/cm2 for 30 s. Compression shear strength glass/glass is 14-18 MPa.","applicationTags":["optical-bonding","uv-curing","glass-bonding","capillary","transparent","modified-acrylate","secondary-heat-cure","dielectric","metal-adhesion","solvent-free"],"cureFamily":"UV acrylate","serviceMax":125,"referenceUrl":"https://www.panacol.com/panacol/datasheets/vitralit/vitralit-6127-english-tds-panacol-adhesive.pdf","viscosityUnit":"mPa.s, Brookfield LVT at 25 C, spindle 2, 60 rpm, test instruction P001","lapShearRangeMPa":[12,17],"lapShear":14.5,"fixtureTime":0.17,"tensileStrengthMPa":20.5,"gapFill":0.05,"cautions":["At least one substrate must be transparent to the recommended wavelength for full UV cure.","Heat curing may only be used as a secondary process for shadowed areas when UV curing is applicable.","Light-sensitive uncured adhesive can begin curing in daylight or longer-term indoor lighting; use 100% light-blocking fluid lines and dispense tips.","Low-surface-energy substrates such as polyethylene and polypropylene must be pretreated for sufficient adhesion.","Published values are typical properties and not product specifications."],"maker":"Panacol","cureDetail":"One-part solvent-free modified acrylate. UV-A discharge-lamp cure is 15 s at 60 mW/cm2 through a 0.05 mm layer; 365 nm LED cure is 10 s at 300 mW/cm2 through a 0.05 mm layer. Secondary heat cure is 40 min at 120 C, and chemical cure with activator is 25 min.","id":"panacol-vitralit-6127","environment":{"humidity":0.45,"fuel":0.25,"immersion":0.25},"summary":"Low-viscosity transparent one-part UV-curing modified acrylate for static glass and optical-component bonding, with capillary action, secondary heat/activator cure options, 20-100 mPa.s viscosity, 17-21 kV/mm dielectric strength and 12-17 MPa glass/aluminum lap shear."},{"profile":"structuralAcrylic","clarity":"opaque","potLife":6,"tdsDocumentLabel":"ITW Performance Polymers Plexus MA300 TDS, last update January 17, 2025","mixRatio":"1:1 by volume and weight","sourceRevisionDate":"ITW Performance Polymers Plexus MA300 TDS, last update January 17, 2025","substrates":{"aluminum":9,"steel":9,"stainless":9,"metal":9,"pcAbs":7,"abs":7,"polycarbonate":7,"pvc":7,"composite":8,"gelcoat":6},"thermalConductivity":null,"tensileStrength":"3510-4290 psi / 24.2-29.6 MPa","stress":{"shear":8,"peel":6,"impact":7},"tdsUrl":"https://itwperformancepolymers.com/wp-content/uploads/Plexus-MA300-TDS.pdf","viscosityClass":"very-high","name":"MA300","viscosityValue":"A: 40000-70000; B: 40000-70000","unpublishedFields":["thermalConductivity"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Aluminum, ASTM D1002, adhesive failure","fixtureTimeRangeMinutes":[11,13],"applicationTags":["structural-bonding","plastic-repair"],"recommendedBondLineMil":"0.01-0.125 in gap tolerance / 0.25-3.2 mm","cureFamily":"Two-part methacrylate structural adhesive","referenceUrl":"https://itwperformancepolymers.com/wp-content/uploads/Plexus-MA300-TDS.pdf","viscosityUnit":"cP","lapShear":21.8,"serviceTemperatureNote":"TDS explicitly recommends application at 65\u201385\u00b0F (18\u201330\u00b0C) for proper cure; temperatures outside that range slow or accelerate cure significantly.","potLifeRangeMinutes":[3,6],"fixtureTime":13,"gapFill":3.2,"cautions":["The TDS gives temperature resistance as a strength-retention graph only; no continuous service temperature range is published.","PC120 Cleaner Conditioner is recommended on metal per the TDS before relying on the headline metal-bond values.","Application at 65-85 F / 18-30 C is recommended; colder or hotter temperatures significantly change cure rate.","Bulk dispensing equipment must be explosion proof; wetted parts should be stainless steel and should avoid brass, carbon steel, copper/copper alloys, Viton, BUNA-N and Neoprene.","Large mixed masses can generate substantial exotherm; dispense only what can be used within working time and keep gaps within max fill.","Chemical resistance is susceptible to strong polar solvents, strong acids and bases."],"maker":"Plexus (ITW)","cureDetail":"1:1 by volume and weight; working time 3-6 minutes at 23 C; reaches about 500 psi in 11-13 minutes and 1000 psi in 13-16 minutes at 23 C","thixotropic":true,"id":"plexus-ma300","summary":"Two-part 1:1 methacrylate structural adhesive for thermoplastic, metal, and composite assemblies, supplied as a non-sagging gel with published 0.25-3.2 mm gap tolerance."},{"profile":"structuralAcrylic","clarity":"opaque","potLife":18,"tdsDocumentLabel":"ITW Performance Polymers Plexus MA310 TDS, last update January 17, 2025","mixRatio":"1:1 by volume and weight","sourceRevisionDate":"ITW Performance Polymers Plexus MA310 TDS, last update January 17, 2025","substrates":{"aluminum":9,"steel":9,"stainless":9,"metal":9,"polyester":5,"pvc":7,"composite":8},"thermalConductivity":null,"tensileStrength":"4410-5390 psi / 30.4-37.2 MPa","stress":{"shear":8,"peel":6,"impact":7},"tdsUrl":"https://itwperformancepolymers.com/wp-content/uploads/Plexus-MA310-TDS.pdf","viscosityClass":"very-high","name":"MA310","viscosityValue":"A: 40000-70000; B: 40000-70000","unpublishedFields":["thermalConductivity"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Aluminum, ASTM D1002, adhesive failure","fixtureTimeRangeMinutes":[38,40],"applicationTags":["structural-bonding","plastic-repair"],"recommendedBondLineMil":"0.01-0.125 in gap tolerance / 0.25-3.2 mm","cureFamily":"Two-part methacrylate structural adhesive","referenceUrl":"https://itwperformancepolymers.com/wp-content/uploads/Plexus-MA310-TDS.pdf","viscosityUnit":"cP","lapShear":23.3,"serviceTemperatureNote":"The official TDS recommends application at 65\u201385\u00b0F (18\u201330\u00b0C) for reliable cure and lists 13\u201325\u00b0C storage range for shelf-life stability.","potLifeRangeMinutes":[15,18],"fixtureTime":40,"gapFill":3.2,"cautions":["The TDS gives temperature resistance as a strength-retention graph only; no continuous service temperature range is published.","PC120 Cleaner Conditioner is recommended on metal per the TDS before relying on the published metal-bond values.","Application at 65-85 F / 18-30 C is recommended; colder or hotter temperatures significantly change cure rate.","Bulk dispensing equipment must be explosion proof; wetted parts should be stainless steel and should avoid brass, carbon steel, copper/copper alloys, Viton, BUNA-N and Neoprene.","Large mixed masses can generate substantial exotherm; dispense only what can be used within working time and keep gaps within max fill.","Chemical resistance is susceptible to strong polar solvents, strong acids and bases."],"maker":"Plexus (ITW)","cureDetail":"1:1 by volume and weight; work time 15-18 minutes at 23.9 C; time to 50 psi 38-40 minutes, 500 psi 44-46 minutes, and 1000 psi 48-50 minutes at 23.9 C","thixotropic":true,"id":"plexus-ma310","summary":"Medium-curing 1:1 methacrylate structural adhesive for thermoplastic, metal, and composite assemblies, supplied as a non-sagging gel with published 0.25-3.2 mm gap tolerance."},{"profile":"structuralAcrylic","clarity":"opaque","potLife":25,"tdsDocumentLabel":"Plexus MA1025 Technical Data Sheet Rev 09, May 2018","serviceMin":-40,"mixRatio":"10:1 by volume; 9:1 by weight","sourceRevisionDate":"Plexus MA1025 Technical Data Sheet Rev 09, May 2018","substrates":{"abs":7,"acrylic":7,"frp":9,"gelcoat":9,"pvc":7,"polyester":9,"dcpdModifiedPolyester":8,"styrenic":7,"urethane":7,"vinylEster":8,"thermoplastic":8,"metal":7,"composite":9},"thermalConductivity":null,"tensileStrength":"1400-1800 psi / 9.7-12.4 MPa","stress":{"shear":6,"peel":7,"impact":8},"tdsUrl":"https://itwperformancepolymers.com/wp-content/uploads/umb/1165/ma1025-data-sheet_rev09.pdf","viscosityClass":"very-high","name":"MA1025","unpublishedFields":["thermalConductivity","viscosityValue","viscosityUnit"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Cohesive strength ASTM D1002, 8.3-13.8 MPa (1200-2000 psi); no specific substrate listed","fixtureTimeRangeMinutes":[40,45],"applicationTags":["structural-bonding"],"recommendedBondLineMil":"0.08-1.00 in gap filling / 2-25 mm","cureFamily":"Two-part methacrylate structural adhesive","serviceMax":82,"referenceUrl":"https://itwperformancepolymers.com/wp-content/uploads/umb/1165/ma1025-data-sheet_rev09.pdf","lapShearRangeMPa":[8.3,13.8],"lapShear":8.3,"potLifeRangeMinutes":[20,25],"fixtureTime":45,"gapFill":25,"cautions":["The official sheet reports tensile and lap-shear as ranges, so those metrics remain in text rather than being collapsed into synthetic point estimates.","Chemical resistance notes explicitly say the product is susceptible to polar solvents and strong acids or bases.","This product is designed around thick marine bond lines and large fiberglass assemblies rather than thin precision joints.","Plexus adhesive Part A is flammable and contains methacrylate esters; keep away from heat, sparks and open flames.","Large mixed masses can generate substantial exotherm and release entrapped air, steam or volatile gases; dispense only what can be used within working time and keep gaps within max fill.","Application at 65-85 F / 18-30 C is recommended; colder or hotter temperatures significantly change cure rate.","Avoid copper/copper alloys in dispensing contact parts; use stainless steel wetted parts and avoid Viton, BUNA-N, Neoprene and other elastomer seals.","ITW recommends substrate testing under anticipated service conditions."],"maker":"Plexus (ITW)","cureDetail":"10:1 by volume; working time 20-25 minutes; fixture time 40-45 minutes at 23 C","thixotropic":true,"id":"plexus-ma1025","summary":"Low-odor, low-shrink two-part 10:1 methacrylate adhesive for structural bonding in marine and composite assemblies with bond lines up to 25 mm thick."},{"profile":"structuralAcrylic","clarity":"opaque","potLife":5,"tdsDocumentLabel":"Plexus (ITW) MA205HV Technical Data Sheet","serviceMin":null,"mixRatio":"10:1 by volume; 9:1 by weight","substrates":{"aluminum":9,"paintedAluminum":4,"smc":5,"coatedMetal":6,"chromatedSteel":6,"metal":8,"thermoplastic":8,"polycarbonate":8,"composite":8},"tensileStrength":"1980-2420 psi / 13.7-16.7 MPa","stress":{"shear":8,"peel":6,"impact":7},"tdsUrl":"https://itwperformancepolymers.com/wp-content/uploads/Plexus-MA205HV-TDS.pdf","viscosityClass":"very-high","name":"MA205HV","viscosityValue":"100000-130000 Part A; 15000-50000 Part B","unpublishedFields":["serviceMin","serviceMax","thermalConductivity","stress","volumeResistivityOhmM","surfaceResistivityOhm","connectionResistanceOhm","insulationResistanceOhm","dielectricConstant","dissipationFactor","dielectricBreakdownVPerMil","dielectricBreakdownKVPerMm","peelStrengthNPerM","chipBondStrengthMPa","cureDepthMm","tackFreeTime"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Aluminum, ASTM D1002, cohesive failure","fixtureTimeRangeMinutes":[7,8],"shelfLifeMonths":10,"applicationTags":["electronics-assembly","structural-bonding"],"recommendedBondLineMil":"0.03-0.25 in gap tolerance","cureFamily":"Two-part methacrylate structural adhesive","serviceMax":null,"referenceUrl":"https://itwperformancepolymers.com/wp-content/uploads/Plexus-MA205HV-TDS.pdf","viscosityUnit":"cP","lapShear":15.9,"serviceTemperatureNote":"No service temperature range stated in TDS; storage temp 13\u201325 \u00b0C (max 38 \u00b0C avoids shelf-life reduction); cure profile shown at 15\u201332 \u00b0C application temperatures.","potLifeRangeMinutes":[3,5],"applicationTemperatureMaxC":30,"applicationTemperatureMinC":18,"fixtureTime":8,"tensileStrengthMPa":13.7,"gapFill":6.4,"cautions":["The TDS gives strength-retention curves by temperature but does not publish a continuous service-temperature range, so serviceMin/serviceMax are intentionally null.","The cached TDS describes MA205HV as non-conductive but does not publish dielectric strength, volume resistivity, or thermal-conductivity values.","PC120 Cleaner Conditioner is recommended on metal before relying on the published metal lap-shear values.","Mixing large masses can generate substantial exotherm and release entrapped air, steam, or volatile gases; confine gap thickness to the published maximum.","Bulk dispensing equipment must be explosion proof; liquid-contact parts should be stainless steel and should avoid brass, carbon steel, copper, copper alloys, Viton, Buna-N, Neoprene, and other elastomer seals."],"maker":"Plexus (ITW)","cureDetail":"10:1 by volume and 9:1 by weight; 3-5 minute work time at 23.9 C and 50 psi handling strength in 7-8 minutes on polycarbonate","thixotropic":true,"id":"plexus-ma205hv","summary":"Fast 10:1 non-conductive methacrylate structural adhesive designed for electronic assemblies, primerless metal bonding, and engineered thermoplastic or composite assemblies with little surface preparation."},{"profile":"structuralAcrylic","clarity":"opaque","potLife":12,"tdsDocumentLabel":"Plexus (ITW) MA8110/GB Technical Data Sheet","serviceMin":null,"mixRatio":"1:1 by volume; 1.01:1 by weight","substrates":{"aluminum":9,"galvanized":9,"zincTreatedSteel":9,"stainlessSteel":9,"carbonSteel":9,"abs":6,"frp":6,"pvc":6,"gelcoat":5,"thermoplastic":8,"composite":8,"metal":9},"tensileStrength":"3285-4015 psi / 22.7-27.2 MPa","stress":{"shear":8,"peel":6,"impact":7},"tdsUrl":"https://itwperformancepolymers.com/wp-content/uploads/Plexus-MA8110_GB-TDS_EN.pdf","viscosityClass":"very-high","name":"MA8110/GB","viscosityValue":"A: 40000-80000; B: 40000-80000","unpublishedFields":["serviceMin","potLife","fixtureTime","lapShear","thermalConductivity","stress"],"lapShearSubstrate":"Aluminum, ASTM D1002, cohesive failure","fixtureTimeRangeMinutes":[44,50],"shelfLifeMonths":12,"applicationTags":["structural-bonding"],"recommendedBondLineMil":"0.01-0.5 in gap tolerance; glass-bead cartridge spacer is 0.012 in","cureFamily":"Two-part methacrylate structural adhesive","referenceUrl":"https://itwperformancepolymers.com/wp-content/uploads/Plexus-MA8110_GB-TDS_EN.pdf","viscosityUnit":"cP","lapShear":21.1,"serviceTemperatureNote":"No service temperature range stated in TDS; storage temp 13\u201325 \u00b0C (max 38 \u00b0C avoids shelf-life reduction); cure profile shown at 15\u201332 \u00b0C application temperatures.","potLifeRangeMinutes":[8,12],"applicationTemperatureMaxC":30,"applicationTemperatureMinC":18,"fixtureTime":50,"gapFill":12.7,"cautions":["The current official TDS gives temperature resistance as a graph only and does not publish a continuous service-temperature range, so serviceMin/serviceMax are intentionally null.","Cartridge products are supplied only with glass-bead spacers; bulk pails and drums are available with or without glass-bead spacers.","Mixing large masses can generate substantial exotherm and release entrapped air, steam, or volatile gases; confine gap thickness to the published maximum.","Bulk dispensing equipment must be explosion proof; liquid-contact parts should be stainless steel and should avoid brass, carbon steel, copper, copper alloys, Viton, Buna-N, Neoprene, and other elastomer seals."],"maker":"Plexus (ITW)","cureDetail":"1:1 by volume and 1.01:1 by weight; 8-12 minute work time at 23.9 C and 1000 psi strength in 44-50 minutes","thixotropic":true,"id":"plexus-ma8110-gb","summary":"Low-halogen 1:1 direct-to-metal methacrylate structural adhesive with optional bulk glass-bead spacer versions and mandatory 0.3 mm glass beads in 50 ml and 400 ml cartridges."},{"profile":"structuralAcrylic","clarity":"opaque","potLife":6,"tdsDocumentLabel":"ITW Performance Polymers TDS last update March 4, 2025","serviceMin":null,"mixRatio":"1:1 by volume; 1.02:1 by weight","sourceRevisionDate":"ITW Performance Polymers TDS last update March 4, 2025","substrates":{"aluminum":9,"stainlessSteel":9,"coldRolledStee